er,\u201d raising concerns about calmness under pressure and crew cohesion.\n**Main trade\u2011off**\nC offers the best balance of calm decision\u2011making and crew\u2011oriented attitude, but his **communication difficulty**, **egocentric perception**, and **reluctance to pursue further education** could hinder effective crew coordination and long\u2011term professional growth.\n**Remaining uncertainty**\n- How severe are C\u2019s communication problems in real flight operations? Could they lead to misunderstandings that outweigh his decision\u2011making strength?\n- Could the negative interpersonal traits of A or D be mitigated by training, or do they pose a greater risk than C\u2019s communication issues?\n**What would change my vote**\n- Concrete evidence that Candidate\u202fA or\u202fD possess strong, proven teamwork and communication skills that offset their interpersonal negatives.\n- Evidence that C\u2019s communication difficulties have resulted in operational errors or cannot be mitigated.\nGiven the current evidence, Candidate\u202fC appears the most suitable overall, though I remain cautious about his communication weakness.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
